This is, I believe, a unique game on market: a realistic, thrilling WWII multiplayer shooter.
PROS:
- SMGs and MGs aren't widely availiable, which is realistic, and dancing with them (firing from the hip) isn't much effective, so no arcade-y shooting, aim if you want to kill. No gun blazing action here;
- A goal attack/defend system which incentives people to play smart instead of going around trigger happy;
- Very immersive with great soundtrack and people "hurrah" when charging, scream when dying;
- A territory/campaign multiplayer, not very influential but gives you a feeling of winning/losing the war and I love it.
- You level playing, then unlock stuff like bayonet to your rifle or bigger magazines to your MGs.
- Role based, if you pick squad leader you must provide support, if you're a commander you must call for artillary, etc. Very top.
- Banzai charge and flamethrower (Rising Storm only).
CONS:
- Some matches you die so much without seeing it coming that it can be frustrating;
- People become devil incarnate if you don't let them drive the tanks;
- Not much populated some hours, so if you don't want to play with bots you end in a server with worse lag;
- Bots are ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥♥ (but can still kill you);
- Game crashes sometimes
- Commie loners roleplaying soviet "heroes", which drives all the sane people to the nazi team most time;
It doesn't have a nice story like Call of Duty: World at War, but it gives that feeling on multiplayer, except that unlike Call of Duty, you can shoot at ALL the socialist ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥s - the nazis and the soviets.
10/10 for quenching my WWII thirst.

TLDR:
Jet Racing Extreme is a simple, fast racing game with well-made damaging and destruction system. It is fun for a little bit but it is not anything special and is not worth its price. I feel like developers wanted to make a good arcade game but then mixed it with realistic damage and destruction system and it didn't match well.
Details:
+ Fast-paced gameplay with nice (but somehow weird) steering. The speed one can reach here is really high and it is exciting;
+ Destruction and damage system - it is very good, detailed thing in this game. You can damage your wheels and even get them completely destroyed and you would still be able to drive your car. That is an interesting and well-made idea;
+ Maps are nice and interesting;
+/- Car upgrades - There are many upgrades available to your vehicle parts which is nice. Although, I somehow had enough money to upgrade everything to its max level after my very first race and I did not even know why. That completely ruined the upgrade system for me. Hopefully they will change it someday in the future;
- Sometimes you could get a feeling that the game is actually too fast - it is very nice to feel the speed but your vehicle always crash after touching literally anything. That is frustrating and I would rather like to enjoy the speed than seeing my car crashing so often in such an arcade game;
- I feel like developer mistakenly mixed 2 different, opposite things in this game - they created realistic game if it comes to damage, destructions and physics but I did not like that - I feel like this game should be a very fast-paced arcade racer in which you could get unbelievable, enormous speeds and enjoy the fast ride without worrying about your car getting crashed that much. Unfortunately, that is impossible - your car gets destroyed everytime it touches something and it frustrates a lot - it completely removes the "arcade" thing;
- Music is repetetive and boring. So are sound effects - honestly they were making me annoyed and I could not stand them after a while;
- In-game purchases - the game itself is a port from mobile game but I try not to judge it by that. However, seeing in-game purchases or "Premium" versions etc. is not good. Only if the game was incredibly cheap but it is not - that is why I am surprised they even kept these in-game purchases in a PC version. That is a big NO;
- Multiplayer seems to be dead. What is even worse, single player mode is boring - you do not even compete with any other AI-controlled cars. You just drive alone;
- Graphics could be better;
Summing up:
I cannot recommend Jet Racing Extreme at its current state. It is not worth the price with what it offers at the moment. It has very good damage and destruction system and physics are nice. However, the thing how developer mixed arcade and realistic style is a big mistake in my opinion. I hope the game will be upgraded and more features will finally be added but as for now, I cannot recommend buying this game, especially for the full price.

